# ============================================================================
# THE ART MASTERS — NOT VERSIONED, AND THAT IS A DECISION RATHER THAN AN OMISSION.
#
# `art/*.jpg` are the Dev's generated playfields at 7x to 9x the size the game
# uses: eighteen megabytes for six pictures, against roughly seventy kilobytes
# each once they are reduced to the playfield. What SHIPS is the reduction, and
# that lives in `app/assets/tables/` and IS versioned.
#
# ⚠️ AND THIS RULE EXISTS BECAUSE I BROKE IT BY ACCIDENT. A `git add -A` swept
# 12.6 MB of masters into a commit about browser tests, whose message did not
# mention them — seventy per cent of the repository's history, added without a
# decision. The commit was undone. A game meant to be cloned onto school machines
# does not carry thirty times its own assets in masters nobody runs.
#
# They are CC0 and they are the Dev's; `art/README.md` records their provenance
# and is versioned. If he wants the masters kept in history, that is his call and
# this block is where it gets reversed.
# ============================================================================
art/*.jpg
art/*.jpeg
art/*.png

# Python bytecode from `scripts/import-art.py`, which runs locally and never in CI.
__pycache__/
